menu "File systems"

config LXFS_V1_UPGRADE
	bool "Upgrade lxfs version 1 in place"
	default y
	help
	  Kernels up to the one that added the lxfs log wrote version 1,
	  which kept file data in the blocks the log now takes.  With this
	  option the first mount moves those blocks and writes version 2;
	  without it a device holding version 1 is left as it is and not
	  mounted.  The upgrade takes about 950 bytes of flash on the AVR,
	  which can be had back once no device holds version 1.

endmenu
